# Wingman exchanges: quiet-moment banter between pilots in formation.

>mothers-street
A[rookie]: I can see my mother's street from here. The whole town, actually.
B[veteran]: Take a good look. It is why we are up here.
A: I will. I will try not to wave.
B: Wave. Nobody is watching but me.

>fuel-six-times
A[rookie]: I have checked my fuel six times. It keeps saying the same thing.
B[veteran]: Then it is probably right.
A: What if it changes while I am not looking?
B: Then you will be the first to know. Check again in ten minutes.

>score-keeping
A[hothead]: That makes four for me this month. I am counting.
B[veteran]: I counted once too. Then I started counting landings instead.
A: Four is still four.
B: Four is fine. Come home for five.

>quiet-pair
A[veteran]: Nice and quiet today.
B[ice]: Yes.
A: You could say more.
B: It is nice. It is quiet.

>the-same-fish
A[joker]: Lunch was a fish that had given up long before I did.
B[veteran]: It was the same fish as yesterday.
A: I thought I recognized the look.
B: Eat it anyway. Dinner is worse.

>as-briefed-day
A[book]: Altitude as briefed. Heading as briefed. Everything as briefed.
B[veteran]: That is a rare day.
A: I am enjoying it very much.
B: So am I. Do not tell anyone.

>why-so-sure
A[rookie]: How do you stay so sure of yourself out here?
B[hothead]: I decided they were scared of me. It helps.
A: And if they are not?
B: Then I find out fast. Stay on my wing.

>afraid-up-here
A[rookie]: Are you ever afraid up here?
B[ice]: Yes.
A: You never sound it.
B: Afraid is a feeling. Flying is a task.

>pay-rumour
A[rookie]: Is it true the pay gets better after the first hundred hours?
B[joker]: The paperwork gets better. The pay is a rumour.
A: Oh.
B: Cheer up. The coffee is free, and it tastes like it.

>landing-by-heart
A[book]: Landing checklist, from the top. Humor me.
B[rookie]: Gear, flaps, hook, lights, harness. Did I miss one?
A: No. That was perfect.
B: Really? I have said it in my sleep for a week.

>too-slow
A[hothead]: You are too slow to start a fight. Everyone says it.
B[ice]: I finish them.
A: That is not the point.
B: It is the only point.

>dessert-bet
A[joker]: A week of dessert says you cannot go an hour without your score.
B[hothead]: Done. Easy. I have four kills.
A: That was eleven seconds. I will collect on Friday.

>hole-in-the-clouds
A[book]: You left the formation again. That was not in the brief.
B[hothead]: The brief did not have a hole in the clouds.
A: The brief had a heading.
B: Fine. Next time I will ask the hole for permission.

>eight-hours
A[joker]: How did you sleep?
B[ice]: Eight hours.
A: Eight. I got three and a mattress that bites.
B: Mine did not bite.

>form-for-the-form
A[joker]: I filed the form for the form I filed last week.
B[book]: Good. The first form requires the second.
A: I was joking.
B: I know. File it anyway.

>greenhouse
A[*]: Hot enough for you down there?
B[*]: The canopy is a greenhouse. I am a tomato.
A: A very brave tomato.

>north-cape
A[*]: We just passed the north cape.
B[*]: That means forty minutes to the strait.
A: And not much more to dinner.

>breathe-out
A[veteran]: Whoever is nervous, breathe out slowly. It works.
B[*]: How did you know?
A: Because I used to be nervous.

>childhood-beach
A[rookie]: That beach down there. I swam there every summer as a kid.
B[*]: It is still there. It will be there after.
A: Yes. I keep telling myself that.

>new-attitude
A[joker]: The ground crew says my airplane needs a new engine, radio and attitude.
B[veteran]: Which one will they actually get you?
A: The attitude. It is the cheapest.

>blackout-town when=night
A[rookie]: There are so few lights down there tonight.
B[veteran]: Blackout. They are being careful.
A: I miss them. The lights.
B: So do they. Keep your eyes out, and we will see them lit again.

>night-is-useful when=night
A[joker]: Night flight. My favorite way to miss both breakfast and dinner.
B[ice]: Dark is useful.
A: To you, everything is useful.
B: Yes.

>anti-collision when=night
A[book]: Anti-collision lights stay off. Please confirm.
B[hothead]: Off. Nobody sees me anyway.
A: That is the idea.
B: I know. I just like being seen.

>harbor-glow when=night
A[veteran]: See that glow on the horizon? That is the harbor town.
B[*]: Still lit?
A: Dim. Somebody is up late with the kettle on.

>better-stars when=night
A[*]: The stars are better tonight.
B[*]: They always are, when nobody can see the island.
A: That is a fair trade.

>sea-and-sky when=night
A[rookie]: I cannot tell where the sea ends and the sky starts.
B[*]: Trust the instruments. Then trust them again.
A: I trust them. I just do not like them.

>wingtip-gone when=rain
A[rookie]: I cannot see my wingtip. Is that normal?
B[book]: In cloud, yes. Instruments only. Stay on the numbers.
A: Staying. Saying them out loud.
B: Good. Quietly, please.

>wasted-weather when=rain
A[hothead]: This weather is wasted on us. Perfect cover, and nobody to hide from.
B[ice]: They cannot see either.
A: Then we are even.
B: Even is fine. Stay level.

>free-wash when=rain
A[joker]: Rain on the canopy. The only wash this airplane ever gets.
B[veteran]: Maintenance would say it gets too much.
A: Maintenance says that about everything that breaks.

>harvest-saved when=rain
A[veteran]: Rain on the coast means the harvest is saved. That is something.
B[*]: And the roads will be mud.
A: Mud is a problem for tomorrow.

>cloud-gap when=rain
A[*]: Cloud tops are at twelve thousand. We can climb out.
B[*]: Not yet. Hold altitude and wait for the gap.
A: Holding.

>shaking-hands when=aftercombat
A[rookie]: My hands are still shaking. Is that bad?
B[hothead]: It means you were there. Mine did that too. Still do.
A: You? Really?
B: Do not spread it around.

>one-was-slow when=aftercombat
A[veteran]: Good work back there.
B[ice]: Thank you.
A: Anything you want to say about it?
B: One of them was slow.

>lucky-accident when=aftercombat
A[hothead]: Did you see that? Straight through the wing!
B[joker]: I saw it. I am writing it up as a lucky accident.
A: Write it as skill.
B: The skill box on the form is smudged. It stays an accident.

>debrief-in-the-air when=aftercombat
A[book]: Debrief checklist. Fuel, ordnance, damage. Rookie, report.
B[rookie]: Fuel good, two missiles left, no damage. I think.
A: You think?
B: No damage. I checked twice.

>the-ones-that-mattered when=aftercombat
A[ice]: They are gone.
B[*]: All of them?
A: The ones that mattered.

>sound-off when=aftercombat
A[veteran]: Everyone sound off. Quietly.
B[*]: Here. All good.
A: Good. Take a minute. Then we go home.

>did-that-happen when=aftercombat
A[*]: Did that really just happen?
B[*]: It did. Breathe.
A: I am breathing. Loudly.

>empty-seat when=loss
A[rookie]: His seat is empty on my left. I keep looking.
B[veteran]: I know. Look when you need to.
A: What do I do?
B: Fly. Fly his side of the sky too.

>should-have-been when=loss
A[hothead]: I should have been on his wing.
B[book]: The plan put you where it put you. It was a sound plan.
A: It was a bad plan.
B: Then the fault is in the plan, not in you.

>owed-a-drink when=loss
A[joker]: I owed him a drink. A whole bottle.
B[ice]: Then keep it.
A: Yes. I will.

>say-his-name when=loss
A[veteran]: We will say his name at the base tonight.
B[*]: Yes. All of us.

>last-to-land when=recovery
A[joker]: First round is on whoever lands last.
B[veteran]: Then I will land slowly.
A: That is cheating.
B: It is called experience.

>approach-lights when=recovery
A[book]: Approach checklist complete. Runway in sight.
B[ice]: Lights on.
A: Confirmed. Lights on.
B: Home.

>sleep-steak-sleep when=recovery
A[hothead]: First thing I do is sleep. Then a steak. Then more sleep.
B[veteran]: Steak first. Otherwise you will dream about it.
A: Steak, sleep, steak. A good plan.

>runway-lights-found when=recovery
A[rookie]: I can see the runway lights! There! Straight ahead!
B[joker]: They are in the usual place. We put them there.
A: Sorry. I am just happy.
B: So am I. Hold on to that.

>island-in-sight when=recovery
A[*]: Fuel is tight, but the island is right there.
B[*]: Tight is fine. Keep it smooth.
A: Smooth. Almost home.

>ground-crew-waiting when=recovery
A[book]: The ground crew will have the ramp ready. Do not make them wait.
B[*]: They would wait all night for us.
A: Yes. That is exactly why we do not make them.
